claimed: intent-centroid-reconsidered — the centroid reached 90.0% with forty distilled rows, matching the model tier from four vectors, and every table in this programme was read with the PROBE as the subject. That is not a cosmetic re-reading: at least three conclusions turned on the probe number specifically. The 4B embedder was judged worse because 2560 dimensions cost the PROBE weights it could not fill -- a centroid fits four vectors either way and may not care. The instruction prefix was worth +1.6 to the probe and +3.3 to the centroid, and the default was chosen on the smaller of the two. The learning curve was read as a signal ceiling because both flattened together, which was measured BEFORE distilled data existed and the centroid has since moved ten points. Re-run those three arms with the centroid as the subject and say plainly which conclusions survive.
